{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793509666214947001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"radiated-obscene-pittabird","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":6,"unsigned":8},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"63f00809ef3c35c90b6bb1993b6c5457b9596015e8f53d669c75913cfc20d07b","event_uuid":"c6678b03-ce78-4cc1-9773-e2f5e3904a2e","position":{"commit_sha":"edca669e7d00b5f26f2c94ed36270b5e9bab3307","position":"1793496377818169795-c6678b03-ce78-4cc1-9773-e2f5e3904a2e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"cb6d389b64cffecb42120c7abdc9bf356b4d428e9dc22623735591bbf128fb2f","event_uuid":"3ca3a9b1-b9a8-4a61-8565-2e0e5d1810a9","position":{"commit_sha":"02422be4c3086e75741cf2aff36ac840a3886c19","position":"1793496556717965150-3ca3a9b1-b9a8-4a61-8565-2e0e5d1810a9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"17e57d21e223357b3e667072f0719e79b570a8214c27e4a144035c9aa03febae","event_uuid":"7449722a-b141-4c76-9030-6e892828ecde","position":{"commit_sha":"a1a11172c04f7f9927ddaadfe721c529a22460fe","position":"1793501428329051064-7449722a-b141-4c76-9030-6e892828ecde"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pre-sweep against origin/main d74d53a5ffd before spending a gate slot. Every line citation in the Approach table was re-measured; 9 defects found and fixed.\n\nCounting error, in three places. The title, the Context sentence and AC1 all said 'nine ADRs', but the Approach table has ten rows and the Scope lists ten files (0012, 0031, 0048, 0059, 0079, 0085, 0105, 0109, 0112, 0113). AC1 was therefore unsatisfiable as written against its own scope. All three now say ten.\n\nFour citations into infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md were wrong; that file has grown since the plan was written. Measured headings: 'The reconciler cursor' is at :252 (plan said :159); 'Kill-switch: revert the LLM path from Bedrock to direct Anthropic' at :374 (plan said :281, and the plan also truncated the heading text); 'Continuous auto-deploy (epic 88ab / story 8903)' at :522 with its Back-out paragraph at :563 (plan said a Back-out paragraph at :470-475, which is actually unrelated ANTHROPIC_API_KEY/fetch-secrets prose).\n\nADR 0112's cap-procedure anchors were all four wrong: :909 and :1141 are blank lines and :1028 is a table row mid-section. The four '## … (ADR 0112 / story …)' sections are at :876, :1008, :1127, :1240.\n\ndocs/config.md cites ADR 0112 at :657 and :676, not :678 and :697.\n\nThe Context runbook inventory omitted gerrit-object-store-repair — 20 listed, 21 present.\n\nsso-auth-host.md '## Secrets' is at :67, not :66 (:66 is the blank line above it).\n\nVerified correct and left alone: 0012:34-36 and :105-108; provision-restore.md §'Provision from scratch' :88; 0048:51-54; 0079:61-65; 0031:158 '### Operator break-glass'; 0105:94-97; ssm-secret-write-only.md:83; 0109:112 and :125; 0113:85 and :95; 0112:241 '## Open items'; 0059:613 and :666; bedrock-access.md:133; run_live_matrix.py:2 'ADR 0037 §4'; test_llm_model_env_removal.py:115 does scan review-bot-ops.md and its node test_no_prose_doc_advertises_the_variable_as_live is at :99; all ten ADR files and all five test targets exist. Epic 6202-e1c7 is confirmed closed, so the 0112 'Open items — resolved' claim holds.","timestamp":1793477493533989001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pre-sweep of this plan against `origin/main` 757ca4852d7, before claiming.\n\n**16 of 16 ADR line ranges verified exact**: 0012 `:34-36`/`:105-108`; 0048 `:30-33`/`:51-54`/`:68-70`; 0079 `:61-65`; 0105 `:94-97`; 0059 `:613-633`/`:666-693`; 0109 `:112-123`/`:125-139`; 0113 `:85-93`/`:95-109`; 0112 `:241-252`.\n\n**Content anchors verified**: 0031 `### Operator break-glass` at `:158`; 0085 `### 3. Eventual-consistency discipline for live probes` at `:58` and `### 4. Report` at `:73`. The `ADR 0037` docstring in `scripts/run_live_matrix.py` is present, 0112's `## Open items` heading is present, and both new runbooks are correctly absent.\n\n**11 of 12 runbook target anchors verified**: `provision-restore.md:88`, `sso-auth-host.md:67`, `review-bot-ops.md` `:252`/`:374`/`:522`/`:563`/`:876`/`:1008`/`:1127`/`:1240`, `bedrock-access.md:133`.\n\n**One citation defect found and corrected.** The 0105 row cited `infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md` §REMEDIATE at `:83`. Line 83 is `### GitHub Actions mirror sync`, a subsection of §ROTATE — not the remediation procedure. §REMEDIATE is `## REMEDIATE the existing exposure (one-time operator cutover)` at `:140-185`. The description now cites `:140-185`.\n\n**Two substantive claims verified rather than assumed:**\n- The 0105 replacement text asserts the one-time cutover ran under task `gnarly-sinistrous-groundhog` (`097b-de23-bf12-4c38`). That ticket is **closed** — the assertion is true.\n- The 0112 replacement asserts the Open items are all resolved via S1–S6 of epic `6202-e1c7-c57f-4897`. All **9** children of that epic are **closed**, S1–S6 included.\n\n**Description compressed 8,363 → 7,639 chars** to clear the 8,000-char plan-review admission cap (`verify.max_ticket_description_chars`) — the plan was already over at 8,287 and could not have been admitted for review as written. The cuts are editorial only: the reproducible `git ls-tree` runbook inventory is replaced by its count, the citation-correction note above moved here, and the S3-ordering note was tightened without dropping any instruction.\n\nReview is deferred until `8257-3a28-e757-4079` closes — this story `depends_on` it, so `review-plan` would fast-fail INDETERMINATE while it is open. The 0031 and 0085 ranges must be re-measured against the post-`8257` tree as the first implementation step, exactly as the plan directs.","timestamp":1793496556717965150},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Post-`8257` re-measurement of the 0031 and 0085 ranges — the first implementation step, done ahead of the claim.\n\nThe plan directs that the 0031 and 0085 citations be re-measured after `8257-3a28-e757-4079` runs, because those are the table's only two rows inside S3's 20-ADR set and S3's archive banner shifts every line below it. Measured against the `impl-8257` working tree (base `757ca4852d7`, with S3's edits applied and not yet landed).\n\nBoth files shift by exactly **+2 lines** — S3 adds 4 lines and removes 2 in each (`git diff --stat`: `4 +++-` on both).\n\n**ADR 0031** — `### Operator break-glass`\n\n| | Pre-S3 (plan as written) | Post-S3 (measured) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Heading | `:158` | `:160` |\n| Section | `:158-165` | `:160-167` |\n| Blank | `:166` | `:168` |\n| Next heading `## Lease self-healing (C2 — extends this module)` | `:167` | `:169` |\n\nLast content line is `:167`, \"lease interval automatically.\" The section's end is still 1 line clear of the next heading, so the hazard the earlier sweep caught — a range running 3 lines past the end and decapitating `## Lease self-healing` — does not reappear at the corrected range.\n\n**ADR 0085** — the two procedural sections\n\n| | Pre-S3 (plan as written) | Post-S3 (measured) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `### 3. Eventual-consistency discipline for live probes` | `:58-71` | `:60-73` |\n| `### 4. Report` | `:73-79` | `:75-81` |\n| Next heading `## Consequences` | `:81` | `:83` |\n\n§3's last content line is `:73` (\"already-gone key re-raises the same eventual-consistency false-failure\"), `:74` is blank, and §4's last content line is `:81` (\"durable evidence … is recorded on ticket d01e\"), `:82` blank.\n\nTwo caveats, stated rather than assumed:\n\n1. These are measured against `8257`'s **unlanded** working tree. `8257` has passed its ACs and gates but has not yet been through `make verify`, Gerrit, or submit. If it changes before landing, re-measure; the +2 offset is a measurement, not a rule.\n2. The plan's instruction to anchor on **content** rather than line number still governs. These numbers are a convenience for the diff review, not a substitute for locating the headings at implementation time.\n\nThe other 7 ADRs in the table (0012, 0048, 0059, 0079, 0105, 0109, 0113) are outside S3's set and are unaffected; the previous sweep verified all 16 of their ranges exact at `757ca4852d7`.\n","timestamp":1793501428329051064}],"created_at":1788808142874048844,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e0a5e20f-bab1-43ec-acb7-c7555311f177","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"8257-3a28-e757-4079"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nTen ADRs carry operator procedure alongside their decision. `infra/runbooks/` already holds 21 runbooks (`git ls-tree origin/main -- infra/runbooks`). Most procedures already exist there in fuller form; the ADR copies are the drift.\n\n## Approach\n| ADR | Procedural lines (origin/main) | Target | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0012 | `:34-36` bootstrap teardown caution; `:105-108` two-step apply + seven secrets | existing `infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md` §\"Provision from scratch\" (`:88-113`) | add the teardown caution to step 1; replace ADR `:105-108` with `See infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md §\"Provision from scratch\".` |\n| 0048 | `:30-33` import mechanics, `:51-54` state-rm + `RE-HOMED-TO-REBAR.md` marker, `:68-70` operator follow-ups | existing `infra/runbooks/sso-auth-host.md`, new section `## Re-homing mechanics (from ADR 0048)` placed before `## Secrets` (`:67`) | move; ADR keeps decision clauses 1–6 as one sentence each + pointer |\n| 0079 | `:61-65` Back-out incl. \"units ship DISABLED; enable after a manual dry-run\" | existing `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md` §\"Continuous auto-deploy (epic 88ab / story 8903)\" (`:522`), whose `**Back-out (disable auto-deploy):**` paragraph is at `:563` | add the ship-disabled/dry-run sentence there; ADR `## Back-out` body → pointer. Amendments (`:74-128`) stay (rationale). |\n| 0085 | `:58-71` eventual-consistency discipline, `:73-79` report procedure | NEW `infra/runbooks/reconciler-live-matrix.md` (how to run `scripts/run_live_matrix.py`, `pytest -m live`, env vars, report paths, index-lag rules, leak log) | move; ADR keeps §1–§2 + pointer. Also fix `scripts/run_live_matrix.py:2` docstring \"ADR 0037 §4\" → \"ADR 0085 (archived into ADR 0121 §20); runbook infra/runbooks/reconciler-live-matrix.md\". |\n| 0031 | `:158-165` Operator break-glass (clear a wedged `refs/reconciler/lock`) | existing `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md` §\"The reconciler cursor\" (`:252`) | move the two commands; ADR keeps pointer (the only procedure inside the consolidation set). CORRECTED: this row previously cited `:158-168`, 3 lines past the section's end, which swallows the `## Lease self-healing (C2 — extends this module)` heading at `:167` — deleting that range would have silently decapitated the next section. The section is `:158-165`; `:166` is blank. |\n| 0105 | `:94-97` \"A one-time operator cutover is required… Until that runs…\" | existing `infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md` §REMEDIATE (`:140-185`) already holds the procedure | replace the bullet with `The one-time cutover ran — task gnarly-sinistrous-groundhog (097b-de23-bf12-4c38); procedure and scrub: infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md §REMEDIATE.` |\n| 0109 | `:112-123` tier-selection table (already single-sourced at `docs/plan-review-gate.md` §\"Validating a gate change: which replay tier\"), `:125-139` cost table | NEW `infra/runbooks/plan-review-eval-ops.md` §\"Replay tiers: invocation and budget\" (`python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0|tier1|tier2 …`, cost table, cap/ledger) | move cost table; replace §6 table with pointer to the gate doc; keep §6's \"required, not advisory\" sentence and the `plan-review-eval:` trailer convention |\n| 0113 | `:85-93` change-triggered execution (`eval-changed-rubrics` job, `.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml:54`), `:95-109` heal-loop schedule + `unreliable-criterion:` ticket handling | same NEW `infra/runbooks/plan-review-eval-ops.md` §\"Heal loop and the unreliable-criterion breaker\" (`rebar criteria heal [--dry-run]`, ledger `.rebar/fixture_heal_ledger.jsonl`, how a human resolves a breaker ticket) | move the operating steps; ADR keeps decisions 6–7 as rules + pointer |\n| 0112 | `:241-252` Open items (all resolved: S1–S6 children of epic `6202-e1c7-c57f-4897` closed; cap procedures at `review-bot-ops.md:876,1008,1127,1240` — the four `## … (ADR 0112 / story …)` sections — and `gate-scratch-mount.md`) | existing runbooks (no new text) | replace `## Open items` with `## Open items — resolved` naming the closing story per item and the runbook sections; keep Decisions 1–7 verbatim (cited by number from `infra/scripts/*.sh`, `docs/config.md:657,676`) |\n| 0059 | `:613-633` §8 Bedrock model-id trap set; `:666-693` §10 compose line anchors and the \"read d2ce before quoting\" status | existing `infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md` §\"Which model id to use\" (`:133`) gets the trap list; `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md` §\"Kill-switch: revert the LLM path from Bedrock to direct Anthropic\" (`:374`) gets the current-wiring paragraph | move; ADR keeps one-sentence findings + pointers. Write \"the removed `REBAR_LLM_MODEL`\" in the runbook (`tests/unit/test_llm_model_env_removal.py:115-150` scans `review-bot-ops.md` for removal context). §9 and \"Evidence-hygiene rules\" stay (findings, not procedure). |\n\nNew runbooks use current vocabulary only (`bridge status`, never `bridge-status`: `test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py` does not history-exempt `infra/runbooks/`) and cite modules/CLI, never `docs/experiments/...` paths (eval-harness epic moves them).\n\n## Scope\nEdit ADRs: `docs/adr/0012-iac-foundations.md`, `0031-reconciler-ref-lock.md`, `0048-rehome-snap-shared-infra.md`, `0059-llm-provider-seam-and-support-tiers.md`, `0079-autodeploy-on-box-timer.md`, `0085-reconciler-live-validation-harness.md`, `0105-ssm-secrets-never-in-terraform-state.md`, `0109-plan-review-replay-harness.md`, `0112-on-box-disk-ceiling-architecture.md`, `0113-fixture-mining-and-admission-protocol.md`. Edit runbooks: `infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md`, `sso-auth-host.md`, `review-bot-ops.md`, `ssm-secret-write-only.md`, `bedrock-access.md`. New: `infra/runbooks/reconciler-live-matrix.md`, `infra/runbooks/plan-review-eval-ops.md`. Also `scripts/run_live_matrix.py` (docstring).\n\n## Testing\n`python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check` (runbook links resolve); `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py`; `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check`; `python scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py`; `pytest tests/unit/test_llm_model_env_removal.py::test_no_prose_doc_advertises_the_variable_as_live tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_docs.py tests/unit/test_det_floor_clarity.py`; `ruff check scripts/run_live_matrix.py`.\n\n**Line numbers for ADRs 0031 and 0085 are measured BEFORE story S3 (`8257-3a28`) runs, and S3 shifts them.** They are the table's only rows inside S3's 20-ADR set; S3 rewrites each original's status line and inserts an archive banner above the body, shifting every line below it. This story runs after S3, so those citations will NOT hold against the tree it edits. Anchor on content: locate the `### Operator break-glass` heading in 0031, and the `### 3. Eventual-consistency discipline for live probes` and `### 4. Report` headings in 0085, taking each section through to the line before the next `#`-prefixed heading. Re-measure and restate those 3 ranges as the first implementation step. The other 7 ADRs in the table (0012, 0048, 0059, 0079, 0105, 0109, 0113) are outside S3's set, so their line numbers are unaffected. The 0085 ranges `:58-71` and `:73-79` were re-measured today and are correct as written against the pre-S3 tree.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] For each of the ten listed ADRs, `grep -c 'infra/runbooks/' docs/adr/<file>` ≥ 1 and the moved line ranges above no longer appear (`git diff -U0` shows them removed).\n- [ ] The two new runbooks exist and every `](…)` in them resolves (`check_docs_index.py --check` exit 0).\n- [ ] `grep -n 'ADR 0037' scripts/run_live_matrix.py` is empty; `grep -n 'Open items$' docs/adr/0112-*.md` is empty.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/0012-iac-foundations.md","reason":"procedure -> pointer"},{"path":"docs/adr/0031-reconciler-ref-lock.md","reason":"break-glass -> pointer"},{"path":"docs/adr/0048-rehome-snap-shared-infra.md","reason":"mechanics -> pointer"},{"path":"docs/adr/0059-llm-provider-seam-and-support-tiers.md","reason":"trap set + wiring -> pointers"},{"path":"docs/adr/0079-autodeploy-on-box-timer.md","reason":"back-out -> pointer"},{"path":"docs/adr/0085-reconciler-live-validation-harness.md","reason":"report procedure -> pointer"},{"path":"docs/adr/0105-ssm-secrets-never-in-terraform-state.md","reason":"cutover bullet -> ran + pointer"},{"path":"docs/adr/0109-plan-review-replay-harness.md","reason":"cost table -> runbook"},{"path":"docs/adr/0112-on-box-disk-ceiling-architecture.md","reason":"open items resolved"},{"path":"docs/adr/0113-fixture-mining-and-admission-protocol.md","reason":"heal-loop ops -> runbook"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md","reason":"teardown caution"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/sso-auth-host.md","reason":"re-homing mechanics section"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md","reason":"back-out sentence, ref-lock break-glass, LLM wiring"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md","reason":"cutover-ran note"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md","reason":"model-id trap set"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/reconciler-live-matrix.md","reason":"new"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/plan-review-eval-ops.md","reason":"new"},{"path":"scripts/run_live_matrix.py","reason":"docstring ADR ref"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","8257-3a28-e757-4079"],["parent","cdac-532f-0edb-422d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"cdac-532f-0edb-422d","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_id":"6acd-24cc-8479-4db8","ticket_type":"story","title":"Move operator procedures out of ten ADRs into infra/runbooks with pointers left behind","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1c73fd95-247e-43b4-8dec-de247635923c","347a1646-7ff6-46b9-b12c-714ad6ec47f2","e6c80b61-4b3c-4bf9-94ae-bdcf459259cd","51031d64-4d56-4476-9f85-e2944955a644","5e1ec982-0311-4688-89df-11cc5ebde20a","b7f687c0-e25e-475f-a3cf-f7bcc71ab671","c6678b03-ce78-4cc1-9773-e2f5e3904a2e","5dea0e47-d282-4fac-bdbe-da16003d06c3","62afe47a-a88e-42e3-8e62-ae6ce40686f4","3ca3a9b1-b9a8-4a61-8565-2e0e5d1810a9","7449722a-b141-4c76-9030-6e892828ecde"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793509666214947001,"uuid":"de3798b2-8098-468d-979d-303774dff5b9"}